---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import profile from '../data/profile.json';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="About"
  description="George Sterpu: AI engineer, PhD, runner, and reader based in Bray, Ireland."
>
  <header class="page-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">About me</p>
    <h1>
      Research, software,
      <br />
      <em>and people.</em>
    </h1>
    <p>
      I’m George Sterpu, an AI engineer with a PhD from Trinity College Dublin.
      My background is in speech and multimodal learning. These days, I work on
      machine learning for building automation at Honeywell.
    </p>
  </header>
  <div class="about-grid">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>How I got here</h2>
      <p>
        During my PhD at Trinity, I researched how sound and mouth movements can
        help a model recognise speech. I proposed{' '}
        <a href="/work/av-align/">AV Align</a>, developed Taris for online
        decoding, and shared the implementations as open-source projects. That
        research led to seven first-author papers, including follow-up journal
        work published in 2022.
      </p>
      <p>
        At Xperi, I developed{' '}
        <a href="/work/edge-speech/">
          speech recognition for a low-power processor
        </a>
        . At Herbst Software, I moved closer to customers, combining product
        management with development, DevOps, and support. At Honeywell, I now
        work on{' '}
        <a href="/work/building-automation/">building models and automation</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Why forward deployed engineering?</h2>
      <p>
        I want to bring those experiences together: understand a customer’s
        problem, work through the technical constraints, build with the people
        who will use the system, and carry the work through to deployment.
      </p>
      <p>
        Working in support made the human side of software much more concrete
        for me. I want to keep that connection as I continue working in AI.
      </p>
      <h2>Outside work</h2>
      <p>
        I’m part of Bray Runners and enjoy participating and volunteering at
        parkrun. Running gives me a sense of progress and community. Reading
        brings in perspectives from business, psychology, science, and lives
        very different from my own.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site is a place for both sides: the engineering work and the things
        that keep me curious.
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside class="about-aside">
      <img
        src="/img/profile_pic.jpg"
        width="800"
        height="800"
        alt="George Sterpu"
      />
      <p class="mono">Bray, Ireland / EU citizen</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/cv/">
        View my résumé <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href="/publications/">
        Research & publications <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={profile.github}>
        Open source on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </aside>
  </div>
  <section class="section-block">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The path so far</p>
        <h2>Experience.</h2>
      </div>
      <a class="text-link" href="/cv/">
        Full résumé <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="experience-list">
      {profile.experience.map((item) => (
        <div class="experience-row">
          <p class="mono">{item.period}</p>
          <div>
            <h3>{item.company}</h3>
            <p class="experience-role">{item.role}</p>
            <p>{item.description}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
